            1721                     !c!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
            1722                     !
            1723                     !c--- the above changed environment is now used to calulate the
            1724                     !c--- effect the arbitrary cloud (with unit mass flux)
            1725                     !c--- would have on the stability,
            1726                     !c--- which then is used to calculate the real mass flux,
            1727                     !c--- necessary to keep this change in balance with the large-scale
            1728                     !c--- destabilization.
            1729                     !
            1730                     !c--- environmental conditions again, first heights
            1731                     !
            1732                     !> ## Using the updated temperature and moisture profiles that were modified by the convection on a short time-scale, recalculate the total cloud work function to determine the change in the cloud work function due to convection, or the stabilizing effect
            1733                     !! - Using notation from Pan and Wu (1995) \cite pan_and_wu_1995, the previously calculated cloud work function is denoted by \f$A^+\f$. Now, it is necessary to use the entraining/detraining cloud model ("static control") to determine the cloud work funct
            1734                     !! - Recalculate saturation specific humidity.
            1735     1                     do k = 1, km
                                   <<< Loop-information Start >>>
                                   <<<  [OPTIMIZATION]
                                   <<<    PREFETCH(HARD) Expected by compiler :
                                   <<<      asqecflg
